=== config ===

CONFIGURATION COMMANDS:
  config output [path]                   Show/set output path
  config depth [n]                       Show/set max depth (1-20)
  config linenumbers ON|OFF              Show/set line numbers
  config color ON|OFF                    Show/set color output
  config threads [n]                     Show/set thread count
  config history [on|off|path]           Show/set history
  config autosuggest ON|OFF              Show/set autosuggest (ghost text)
  config idle ON|OFF                     Show/set the ghost typing idle hint
  config git ON|OFF                      Enable/disable git integration (prompt + symbols)
  config dir_view ON|OFF                 Show/hide directory tree in shell
  config intro_view ON|OFF               Show/hide the startup logo, ntpkg and watcher notices (alias: iv)
  config file_view ON|OFF                Include files in automatic navigation tree (alias: fv)
  config todo format <txt|md|json|toml|yaml|html>
    Set the todo file format
  config size all|file|dir ON|OFF        Auto-calculate sizes in navigation tree; uses --care (alias: s)
  config watch ON|OFF                    Enable/disable file watcher
  config watch trigger <a>               Auto-run alias when watcher fires
  config watch trigger off               Disable auto-run
  config watch limit <n>                 Rows shown in watcher change box
  config qsc "#c 0"                      Set QSC global hotkey
  config qsc off                         Disable QSC hotkey
  config lang [language]                 Show/set interface language
  config env NAME value [-g|-l|-os|-osg] Set an NTC env var (NAME=value also works; bare: list; NAME alone: show)
    -g global | -l local | -os this session | -osg persist to OS
    default: local if ntconfig.toml exists, else global
  config rmenv NAME [-g|-l|-os|-osg|-all]
    Remove an NTC env var (-all: every store + session)
  config serve [service] [--port-default N] [--bind-default ADDR]
    Per-service serve defaults (CLI; `serve config` is the browser GUI)
  config update_check ON|OFF             Show/hide daily new-release notice (alias: uc)
  config integration_shell ON|OFF        Complete installed shell names (powershell on Windows, bash on Linux desktop, cmd, …), their launcher flags, and enable interactive ntc ps on Windows / ntc <distro> on Linux (alias: is)
  config code_tools ON|OFF               Complete installed programming tools/compilers (g++, python, java, cargo, …) and their flags (alias: ct)
Examples:
    config output ~/Desktop                # Set output path to Desktop
    config depth 3                         # Set max depth to 3
    config color ON                        # Enable color output
    config threads 8                       # Set thread count to 8
