    cvcode b64 "aGVsbG8=" to plaintext     # Decode to readable text
=== deadlock ===

DEADLOCK - encrypted password vault:
  deadlock                               Open the vault (asks for the master password)
  ls                                     List every pass-env with its real password
  add <pass-env> <real-password>         Store or update a secret (password may be quoted)
  rmpw <pass-env>                        Delete a stored secret
  master-pass                            Change the master password
  forget                                 Remove the master password from the OS credential store
  destroy                                Delete the vault and every stored secret
  exit                                   Close the vault and return to the ntc shell
Secrets are encrypted with AES-256-GCM under an Argon2id key derived from the master password. The default master password is 12345678 and deadlock asks for a new one on first login. The vault file is restricted to your user account and is protected against deletion by the OS (Windows deny-DELETE ACL / macOS uchg; Linux needs root). The master is registered in the OS credential store so nssh can resolve pass-env names without opening this shell.
Examples:
    deadlock
    deadlock > add prod_pass CatLoveFish360@house
