=== gs ===

GS COMMAND:
  gs <pattern> [-p <glob>] [-s [line|path|size]] [-d <n>] [-l <n>] [-A <n>] [-B <n>] [-I] [-x] [-h|-g|-w] [-z]
    Search file contents (simple grep)
  gs -I [pattern] [-d <n>]               Interactive grep (10/page, f=pattern, e/Enter=open, 0-9=row, ?=keys, x/h/g/w/z=toggles)
  cmd | gs <pattern>                     Search piped text (qur -s <pattern> too)
  gs <pattern> -A <n> -B <n>             Show n lines after / before each match (10 matches unless -l <n>)
  gs -x <literal> -h <starts> -g <ends> -w <whole> -z <case>
    -x searches the text literally (a\|b is 'a|b', no OR); -h/-g/-w match the trimmed line and can't be combined; -z keeps case
Examples:
    gs fn main                             # Search for 'fn main' in files
    gs -I config                           # Interactive search results
    gs TODO < app.log                      # Search piped/redirected text
    gs error\|warning                      # OR search: match either term (a\|b)
    gs main -A 3 -B 2                      # Match plus 3 lines after and 2 before
    gs -w main                             # Only lines that are exactly 'main'
    gs -z Main -h                          # Case-sensitive: lines starting with 'Main'
