=== http ===

HTTP COMMAND:
  http <method> <url> [options]          Send a request (method defaults to GET)
  http GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE|HEAD|QUERY <url>
    Supported methods
  Options: -H "Key: Value" header, -d text body, --json JSON body (sets Content-Type), -q key=value query param, -a user:pass Basic auth, --bearer token, -o file save the body, -s print only the body, -v show the request, -t seconds timeout (default 30). JSON responses are pretty-printed unless --no-pretty is given.
Examples:
    http GET https://api.example.com/users # Simple GET request
    http POST https://api.example.com/users --json '{"name":"ada"}' # POST a JSON body
    http GET https://api.github.com/repos/rust-lang/rust -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" -q per_page=1 # Header + query parameter
    http GET https://api.example.com/me -a user:pass -o me.json # Basic auth, save body to a file
    http GET https://api.example.com/users -s | qur -s name # Pipe the raw body into another command
