=== ral ===

RUN ALIAS COMMANDS:
  ral add <name> "<cmd>"                 Create alias
  ral add <name>(x) "<cmd>"              Create parameterised alias with ${x}
  ral add <name> "<cmd>"                 Bare $NAME is an env var at run time; use ${x} for parameters
  ral add <name>({x=a,e=txt}) "<cmd>"    Alias with default values
  ral add <name>(x[],y) "<cmd>"          Alias with array params
  ral add <name>(x) "echo $*{x}"         One arg with spaces (quotes stripped)
  ral edit <name> "<cmd>"                Update alias
  ral rnm <old> to <new>                 Rename alias
  ral rm <name>[, ...]                   Remove alias(es)
  ral list                               Show all aliases
  ral info <name> [--edit]               Show alias details (--edit: copy edit command to clipboard)
  ral cls                                Clear ALL aliases (with confirmation)
  ral export --all <name>                Export all aliases to <name>.ntc.ral
  ral export --select <name>             Select aliases to export
  ral import <file>                      Import aliases from .ntc.ral file
  ral install                            Install run aliases from the ntc GitHub catalog
  ral make [name]                        Create alias template in CWD
  ral hintn add|rm|rnm|info|ls           Manage named value lists for --hint-n/--select-n
Examples:
    ral add build "cargo build"            # Create simple alias
    ral add greet(x) "echo Hello ${x}"     # Parameterised alias
    ral add v "view --care -t -d ${x:-1}"  # Alias with defaults
    ral list                               # Show all aliases
    ral export --all myaliases             # Export aliases
    ral hintn add port [8080,5050]         # Named list for #x --hint-n port
