=== scan ===

SCAN COMMANDS:
  scan ext <ext...>                      List files by extension (no line counts)
  scan files [pattern]                   List files by name pattern (* = all)
  scan dir [pattern]                     List directories by name pattern (* = all)
  scan ext <ext...> -d, --depth <n>      Limit scan depth
  scan ext <ext...> -s, --size           Show sizes + total
  scan ext <ext...> --care               Include everything (care mode)
  scan port [host] [--top N | --ports <spec> | --all]
    TCP port scan
  scan ip [cidr] [--top N | --ports <spec>]
    Live-host sweep + ARP
  scan pid [[user@]host[:port]|profile] [--sort memory|pid|name] [--filter <text>] [--min-memory <size>] [--max-memory <size>] [--offset <n>] [--limit <n>]
    List processes (nssh profile, host, or local)
  scan waep <host|url>                   Enumerate web paths (/api, /admin, /upload, ...)
  scan waep example.com/api -r -d 2      Recurse under a base path
  scan waep <target> [-w <file>] [-x <ext,...>] [-m GET|HEAD] [-s <codes>] [--all]
    Wordlist, suffixes, method, accepted statuses
  scan waep <target> [-r] [-d 1-4] [-c 1-64] [--timeout <ms>] [-H 'Name: value'] [-A <ua>] [-o <file>] [-q]
    Recursion, speed, headers, output
Examples:
    scan ext rs                            # List all .rs files
    scan ext rs c -d 2                     # List .rs/.c files up to depth 2
    scan ext rs c -s                       # List with sizes + total
    scan port 192.168.1.1 --top 10         # Scan top 10 ports
    scan ip 192.168.1.0/24                 # Sweep for live hosts
    scan files *.rs                        # List files by name pattern
    scan dir k*                            # List directories by name pattern
    scan waep http://127.0.0.1:55555/api   # Discover what an ntc serve API exposes
    scan waep example.com -x php,html --all # Show every response plus .php/.html variants
    scan waep example.com/api -r -d 2 -c 32 # Recurse two levels with 32 parallel probes
