=== time ===

TIME COMMAND - timing, comparison and countdowns:
  time <command>                         Run a command and show how long it took
  time <command A> --compare <command B> [-w]
    Run both and compare exit status + captured output
  time --bench <n> <command>             Repeat n times and show min/max/mean/median
  time --count <duration>                Countdown (e.g. 30, 90s, 5m, 1h30m)
  time --help                            Show this help
  Commands run in the current directory and may be NTC commands, aliases, or external commands. --compare captures output; --bench runs the command n times, so its side effects repeat too. Ctrl+C cancels a countdown.
