  views --sort <name|ext|size>           Sort entries (default: name)
  views -n                               One entry per line instead of the flowing groups
  views --trim <text>                    Remove text from names and the ... group separator (repeatable, keeps colours)
  No [Directory]/[ignored] tags - colours show the kind. Depth is fixed at 1 and sizes are always computed with --care semantics. Use --size to display sizes.
Examples:
    views                                  # Flat listing of the current directory
    views src --size 1KB --sort size       # Entries >= 1KB, largest first, sizes shown
=== where ===

WHERE COMMAND:
  where [-a|--all] [<binary>]            Show the ntc executable, or find a binary on PATH
Examples:
    where -a                               # Show every ntc config, session, package and vault path
    where git                              # Show the first git on PATH (-a lists every match)
=== wi ===

WI COMMAND:
  wi [path]                              Live file-change feed (q=quit)
Examples:
    wi                                     # Watch file changes live
